{
  "description": "The feed's orders. `sort` (absent means `newest`) orders a whole list of `items`; `expected` is their ids in order. Every order ends in the same tie-break: newest first by `publishedAt` (RFC 3339 UTC strings from YouTube, compared as plain ASCII strings), then by item id (video or playlist id, ASCII order, ascending). `newest`: that tie-break alone. `title`: by `title` (absent here means the id) ignoring case: replace each Unicode code point of both titles, one at a time and with no context, by its locale-independent lowercase mapping (which may be several code points), then compare the results code point by code point (not by UTF-16 unit), a title that is a prefix of the other first; no Unicode normalization; titles equal after lowercasing tie. `shortest`: by `durationSeconds` ascending; items without a duration (a playlist, `kind` \"playlist\" here, or a video whose `durationSeconds` is absent or 0) come after every item with one, tying with each other. `random`: ascending by the 32-bit FNV-1a hash (start 2166136261; for each byte: xor the byte in, then multiply by 16777619 modulo 2^32; compared unsigned) of the UTF-8 bytes of `seed` written in decimal, a colon, and the item id; `seed` is a whole number from 0 to 2^32-1 that a client picks anew at each full load and never syncs, so the order holds until the next full load. The feed is shown in the chosen order once a load has finished; while a load runs the previous feed stays, greyed out.",
